Package: PaPeR
Type: Package
Title: Parentage Assignment for Microhaplotype and SNP Markers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tyler", "Wittman", email = "wittman98@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Claude", role = "ctb",
           comment = "AI model by Anthropic; co-wrote the code and documentation as a coding assistant"))
Description: Assigns genotyped dams and sires to genotyped individuals from
    multiallelic microhaplotype or biallelic SNP genotypes and life-history
    data. Inspired by the parentage step of 'sequoia' (Huisman 2017,
    <doi:10.1111/1755-0998.12665>), whose heuristic search and settings it
    follows, it decides each parent with an exact local pedigree-likelihood
    comparison of the assigned parents against alternative relationships
    (siblings, grandparents, aunts and uncles, half-siblings and others),
    conditioning on the relatives already assigned. Microhaplotype errors use
    a dropout/foreign model and SNP errors the 'sequoia' model; the error rate
    is calibrated from the confident trios of the inferred pedigree. Sibship
    clustering and dummy parents are outside its scope.
